      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Would the ideal solution here not be that we (and Guix) nudge users towards the more secure **unprivileged** solution, and that this worked to build correctly, i.e. the opposite of what you are recommending? Working under the assumption that these failures will be ironed out as the (relatively new) rootless-daemon approach gets more usage/testing.\n\nIf we must choose between one or the other **today** though, and the rootless approach is broken, then I'd agree that perhaps we can detect/warn towards requiring the root approach.\n\nFWIW the nixpkgs [Guix service](https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/modules/services/misc/guix/default.nix) uses the privileged approach, with no built-in option to change.",
